==Trivia==

;{{ci|Galio|Galio, the Sentinel's Sorrow|variant=old3|size=32px}}
* The name Galio may be inspired by the name Galileo, most commonly known for the Renaissance polymath {{w|Galileo Galilei|Galileo}}.
** The name Galileo means "man of {{w|Galilee}}", ultimately from Semitic root {{w|Gilgal|g-l}} "to roll".<ref>Huehnergard, J. ''2011 Proto-Semitic Language & Culture; Semitic Roots'' p. 2073
</ref>
* Galio's dance references {{w|Beauty and the Beast (1991 film)|Beauty and the Beast}} by {{w|Walt Disney}}.

;{{ci|Galio|Galio, the Colossus|size=32px}}
* Galio retains his dance post-[[rework]], which references Beauty and the Beast by Walt Disney.
* He references his previous alias while attacking a {{ui|Blue Sentinel}}: {{sm2|Galio_Original_AttackSentinel_3.ogg}}{{sbc|"You're a sentinel? I'm a sentinel! We should fight!"}}
** In this case however, this interaction has literal implications: Galio being a textbook-definition sentinel for Demacia, and Galio perhaps sharing similar origins with the Blue Sentinel, both being rock/mineral beings empowered/given life by magic.
* {{Self Crowd Control champion|Galio}}

