==Trivia==

;{{ci|Karma|variant=old|image=Karma OriginalSquare old.png|size=32|Karma, the Enlightened One}}
* Karma was named after {{w|Karma|the eponymous cause-and-effect principle}}.
** Her title, ''The Enlightened One'', references {{w|Gautama Buddha}} & {{w|Enlightenment in Buddhism|Awakening}}.
* {{ai|Mantra old|Karma|Mantra}} was named after {{w|Mantra|the eponymous Hindu sacred utterances}}, from {{w|Proto-Indo-Iranian language|Indo-Iranic}} ''*mántram'' < {{w|Proto-Indo-European language|PIE}} ''*{{Tt|men-|think}}<ref>http://www.palaeolexicon.com/Word/Show/28990/</ref>{{Tt|tro-|instrumental suffix}}m'' "instrument of thought".
**  The 'translation' for {{ais|Mantra old|Karma|Mantra}} Ancient Ionian language was provided by Player Support Escalation Specialist 'Marowe'.
* Karma was the first champion to feature an '[[Art Spotlight]]' before release and the first to be [[rework|fully relaunched]].
** She was the fifth to have more than four abilities (the others being {{ci|Elise}}, {{ci|Gnar}}, {{ci|Heimerdinger}}, {{ci|Jayce}}, {{ci|Lee Sin}}, and {{ci|Nidalee}}).
* Like {{ci|Jayce}}, Karma used to have six ranks on each basic ability and only one on her {{ai|Mantra|Karma|ultimate}}.
* {{ais|Renewal|Karma}} root has the longest duration in-game ({{fd|3.25}} seconds with {{ai|Focused Resolve|Karma}} and {{ai|Mantra|Karma}} both fully-ranked).
* In the minigame [[Astro Teemo]], the most expensive upgrade in the game that {{cis|Teemo}} can purchase, Soul Shield, is a reference to one of Karma's pre-rework {{ai|Soul Shield|Karma|skills}} of the same name.

;{{ci|Karma|size=32|Karma, the Enlightened One}}
* In Karma's most current lore, Karma's spirit has lived countless lives only to be re-incarnated within new bodies, inspired by {{w|Reincarnation|the eponynous concept}} in {{w|Indian religions|Dharmic religions}}.
** The name of her current incarnation, ''Darha'', comes from Sanskrit adjective {{Tt|दृढ ''dṛḍhá''|Classical}} < {{Tt|दृळ्ह ''dṛḷhá''|Vedic}} "{{Tt|firm|Latin cognate firmus, from dʰer-mo-s}}, steadfast", sharing {{w|Proto-Indo-European language|PIE}} root ''dʰer-'' "to uphold" with {{ci|Darius|'''''Dar'''''ius}}.<ref>De Vaan, M. ''Etymological Dictionary of Latin'' (2008). p. 223</ref><ref>Cheung, J. ''Etymological Dictionary of Iranian verbs'' (2007). p. 57-59</ref>
* Karma was the fourth champion to feature two '[[Champion Spotlight]]s' due to significant gameplay changes (the others being {{ci|Ezreal}}, {{ci|Katarina}}, {{ci|Lee Sin}}, and {{ci|Sivir}})
*{{ais|Inspire|Karma}} speed buff reads “Vroom Vroom!”.
* Karma, {{ci|Lee Sin}}, {{ci|Sejuani}}, and {{ci|Trundle}} are the only champions to feature a ''[[Universe:Ages_of_Runeterra/Traditional|traditional]]'' skin representing them before their visual updates. {{cis|Viktor}} {{csl|Viktor|Machine Herald|Machine Herald}} skin also represents him before his visual update, but doesn't have "traditional" in the name.

