==Trivia==

* Graves' jokes reference {{w|gallows humor}}, as per his surname ''{{w|Cemetery|Graves}}''.
* Graves' dance references [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=003_ulzGw4I one from a country show].
** A side-by-side comparison can be seen [http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-xlVN_g-nok here].
* Graves was the second-to-last champion to have a "League Judgement" (they were discontinued after release; {{ci|Varus}} was the last champion to receive one).
* {{ai|End of the Line|Graves}} is among a few abilities that were named after a quote of their champion. In this case, it references his "End of the Line" quote which he had before the patch he got the ability, [[V5.22]].
** The others are {{cai|Goes Where He Pleases|Dr. Mundo}} and {{cai|League of Draven|Draven}}.
* The icon for {{ai|Collateral Damage|Graves}} is a reference to explosive hazard safety signs. 
* Graves' shotgun can be seen in the game's [[Mac Client Available|Mac version trailer]].
* Graves was the product of playerbase requests for a 'manly' ranged carry.
* In the Chinese localization, the names of all four of his active abilities are four-character phrases that allude to the criminal underworld and are often titles of gangster or martial arts films or television.
** {{ai|End of the Line|Graves}} becomes 人在江湖, literally "a person in river and lake"; "river and lake" is a euphemism for the underworld, and the phrase is usually used to imply a person in the underworld cannot avoid committing unsavoury actions. Secondary title of ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Young_and_Dangerous Young and Dangerous]'', a Hong Kong triad film, in Chinese.
** {{ai|Smoke Screen|Graves}} becomes 一手遮天, literally "covering the sky with one hand", a phrase to describe a criminal so well-connected and/or powerful they can halt justice. Secondary title of ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Young_and_Dangerous_3 Young and Dangerous 3]'', a sequel to the above, in Chinese.
** {{ai|Quickdraw|Graves}} becomes 猛龙过江, literally "ferocious dragon crossing river", usually used to describe a ruthless foreign rival or criminal. Secondary title of ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Young_and_Dangerous_2 Young and Dangerous 2]'' in Chinese. It is also the Chinese name of ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Way_of_the_Dragon Way of the Dragon]'', starring Bruce Lee who fights against foreign martial artists including Chuck Norris.
** {{ai|Collateral Damage|Graves}} becomes 龙争虎斗, literally "struggle of dragon and tiger", a phrase similar to "clash of the titans" in English. Secondary title of ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Young_and_Dangerous_5 Young and Dangerous 5]'' in Chinese. It is also the Chinese name of ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enter_the_Dragon Enter the Dragon]''.


