==Trivia==
* {{Shapeshifter Champion|Jayce}}
** In Jayce's case, his ultimate ability allows him to switch between the melee {{sbc|{{ai|Transform Mercury Hammer|Jayce|Hammer Stance}}}} and ranged {{sbc|{{ai|Transform Mercury Cannon|Jayce|Cannon Stance}}}}, both having their specific sets of abilities.
* Jayce, {{ci|Elise}}, {{ci|Gnar}}, {{ci|Nidalee}}, and {{ci|Kayle}} are the only champions to be conditionally considered both {{tip|ranged}} and {{tip|melee}}.
* Jayce was the 100th released champion.
* Jayce's release marks:
** The first champion to have access to eight abilities ({{ai|Transform Mercury Cannon|Jayce}} and {{ai|Transform Mercury Hammer|Jayce}} counted separately).
** The third champion to have a dedicated {{si|Recall}} animation on release, the previous ones being {{ci|Darius}} and {{ci|Draven}}.
** The third champion able to start the game with an unlocked Ultimate ability, the previous ones being {{ci|Udyr}} and {{ci|Karma}}. {{ci|Nidalee}}'s ultimate at the time still required level 6.
** The fourth champion to have access to all four abilities at Level 1, the other ones being {{ci|Elise}}, {{ci|Karma}}, {{ci|Nidalee}}, and {{ci|Udyr}}.
* Jayce's dance references [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=otCpCn0l4Wo U Can't Touch This] by {{w|MC Hammer}}.
** A side-by-side comparison can be seen [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vQHI8uWSKF0 here].
** He shares this dance with {{ci|Malzahar}} (specifically his {{ais|Void Swarm|Malzahar|Voidlings}} part).
** Coincidentally, 'Mercury {{ai|Transform Mercury Cannon|Jayce|Cannon}} / {{ai|Transform Mercury Hammer|Jayce|Hammer}}' can be shortened to 'MC Hammer'.
** One of Jayce's Series 2 [[Eternals]]: ''Hammer Time'' also references this.
* Jayce's title, ''"the Defender of Tomorrow"'', likely references {{w|Superman: The Man of Tomorrow}}.
* Jayce was the first champion to have gold-colored spell indicators (in his {{ai|Transform Mercury Hammer|Jayce|Hammer Stance}}).
** He was the only one to do so until {{ci|Mel}} received them in [[V25.04]]

