==Trivia==
* {{Shapeshifter Champion|Gnar}}
** In Gnar's case, {{ai|Rage Gene|Gnar}} transforms him into {{ci|Mega Gnar}}, becoming melee and altering his abilities and statistics.
* Gnar, {{ci|Elise}}, {{ci|Nidalee}}, {{ci|Jayce}}, and {{ci|Kayle}} are the only champions to be conditionally considered both {{tip|ranged}} and {{tip|melee}}.
* Gnar's concept is built on monstrous transformations in fiction coupled with the [http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FishOutOfWater Fish Out of Water] trope.
** Inspirations include {{w|Strange Case of Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde}} by {{w|Robert Louis Stevenson}}, {{w|Gremlins}}, and {{w|Hulk (comics)|Hulk}} by {{w|Marvel Comics}}.
** Paleontologically speaking, Gnar is not a missing link, i.e. {{w|transitional fossil|transitional specimen}}, but he belongs to the Yordle population ancestral to modern ones; colloquially-speaking, he is the great-great-...-granduncle of all living Yordles.
* In Brazilian localization, Gnar's title was changed to ''O Yordle Pré-histórico'' ('the Prehistoric Yordle') in order to avoid matchmaking-rating-associated jokes/bullying derived from ''O Elo Perdido'' ('the Missing Link').
* Gnar is the second champion to have two champion portraits ({{ci|Gnar|Mini Gnar}} and {{ci|Mega Gnar}}) the first being {{ci|Quinn}} and {{ci|Valor}}.
** He is also the third to have more than one chat name, the first being {{ci|Anivia}} and {{ai|Rebirth|Anivia|Eggnivia}} and the second being anyone polymorphed by {{ci|Lulu}} ({{ai|Whimsy|Lulu|Squill}}).
*** As well as the seventh champion to have more than four abilities, the others being {{ci|Elise}}, {{ci|Heimerdinger}}, {{ci|Jayce}}, {{ci|Karma}}, {{ci|Nidalee}}, {{ci|Lee Sin}}, {{ci|Rek'Sai}} and {{ci|Yorick}}.
* Mini Gnar has the fewest active abilities of any ranged champion ({{ai|Hyper|Gnar}} and {{ai|GNAR!|Gnar}} are fully passive effects) and the third lowest health at Level 18 at {{highest lowest stats|hp|sortby=bot|size=1|lvl=18|show=3}}.
* Mega Gnar has his own separate emotes from Mini Gnar's.
** His dance references {{w|Donkey Kong}}.
*** {{ai|Boulder Toss|Gnar}}' projectile is shaped like the [[Riot Games Inc.]] logo.
* Gnar's Series 2 [[Eternals]] make the following references:
** ''Clobberin' Time'' is a reference to the eponymous quote by {{w|Thing (comics)|The Thing}}, a member of the {{w|Fantastic Four}}.
* Mega Gnar has the highest {{as|{{sti|experience|level 18}}}} {{as|{{sti|'''base''' attack damage}}}} at {{highest lowest stats|ad|sortby=top|size=1|lvl=18}}.
* Although patch [[V7.16]] made it so the portrait of the selected skin would be used in the central portion of the in-game UI, transforming into {{ci|Mega Gnar}} always uses his base portrait for all skins.
* {{ai|Hop|Gnar}} has the shortest ability name at 3 characters long.
** For contrast, {{ai|Life Form Disintegration Ray|Vel'Koz}} is the longest ability name at 28 characters long, exceeding {{ai|Hop|Gnar}} by 25 characters.

